  message: "Fixed in PR #2183. The seven ungrouped commands are in a named group (TRUST, CACHE & CATALOGUE COMMANDS) and the heading is looked up with no fallback; --path takes PATH; the eleven tracker IDs and two audit labels are out of the help strings. BEHAVIOUR: 'hypergumbo --help --all' on the merged code has 0 lines with _PATH_FLAG (24 before), no DEFAULT heading, and 0 tracker IDs (15 before). The check asked for: test_cli_help_user_facing_names.py walks the built parser and the rendered help (every subcommand in a named group; no option displays a name beginning with an underscore; no tracker ID), so a later subcommand or option is covered without editing it. The widening noted on this item (tracker IDs) is included."  # 664f
